The review has been written to `/Users/rich/source/HARES/docs/reviews/types-physics/types-physics-12-no-hrv-erv-balanced-mechanical-ventilation.md`.

**Summary of findings (6 total):**

| Severity | Count |
|----------|-------|
| Critical | 1 |
| High     | 2 |
| Medium   | 2 |
| Low      | 1 |

**Critical**: The model is a supply-only effectiveness model, not a true balanced HRV/ERV. The exhaust stream mass flow and its thermal impact (removal of conditioned indoor air) are entirely absent. EnergyPlus models both supply (SupIn→SupOut) and secondary/exhaust (SecIn→SecOut) streams with full heat balance.

**High**: (1) The effectiveness formula omits the `CMin/CSup` capacity rate ratio required by heat exchanger theory. (2) Frost control is a single fixed derating multiplier vs. EnergyPlus's three-mode system with iterative bypass fraction solving, time-varying defrost fractions, and exhaust recirculation.

**Medium**: (1) The `balanced` config flag is passed to the thermal solver but the equipment itself ignores it. (2) Fan power is a single constant value, not separated into supply + exhaust fans, and doesn't vary with defrost/bypass modes.
